        "thinking": "I'm tracing सुख as a curadi root in the kathādi group, which is अदन्त — so adding णिच् gives सुखि without vṛddhi due to a-lopa being sthānivad. Curadi roots are typically ubhayapada since णिच् itself conditions both pada options.\n\nFor the parasmaipada āśīrlin uttama eka-vacana, णi drops before the ārdhadhātuka आशीर्लिङ् ending (णेरनिटि rule), giving सुख्यासम् as the final form — the ātmanepada counterpart would be सुखयिषीय, but सुख्यासम् is the answer I'm settling on.\n\n",
